---
description: Apply Hybrid Native UI v2.0 (Apple glass chrome + Android shared axis/input/switch + hybrid buttons/lists/modals) for layout, animation, and performance.
globs: "*.{css,scss,html,js,ts,tsx,swift,kt,kts,vue}"
alwaysApply: false
---

When building or changing UI, motion, glass, sheets, buttons, lists, theme, input fields, or switches, follow `.cursor/skills/hybrid-native-ui/SKILL.md`.

v2.0 user preferences (authoritative):
- Layout: Apple — glass only on chrome (sidebar/toolbar), content opaque, hairline borders
- Button: Hybrid — hover color darken, active scale(0.98), 150ms ease, NO spring, NO ripple on mouse
- Card: Apple — hover translateY(-3px) scale(1.015) + shadow, 350ms spring
- Page switch: Android — shared axis directional translate, 300ms, incoming decelerate / outgoing accelerate
- List selection: Hybrid — floating pill (white bg + shadow on #F7F7F9 list), 8-10px radius
- Input: Android — filled style, bottom underline + floating label, focus color #6750A4 purple
- Modal: Hybrid — centered scale(0.95)+opacity fade in, 250ms ease
- Switch: Android Material 3 — track #6750A4 when on, thumb #E8DEF8, 250ms translate

Hard rules:
- Animate transform + opacity only. Never animate top/left/width/height/margin.
- Glass on chrome only. Never backdrop-filter on content cards or scrolling content.
- ≤2 live blur regions.
- No `transition: all`.
- Spatial (position/scale) may spring; effects (opacity/color/blur) must tween.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- Read `code/` for copy-paste implementations. Run `node .cursor/skills/hybrid-native-ui/scripts/check-css-motion.mjs <file.css>` on CSS you write.
